# wip — runtime-dx-foundation
# Branch: feature/runtime-dx-foundation
# Started: 2026-02-23

#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Lay a DX foundation across runtime + editor integrations with structured diagnostics, instrumentation hooks, and clear troubleshooting paths."
 ~#taste: "clarity + correctness"
}

^["stream"]{
 # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
 # >>[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <type> — <content>
 >>[2026-02-23 11:15] observe — DX roadmap request includes plugin development, LSP/worker flow, and runtime instrumentation.
 >>[2026-02-23 11:18] decide — Start with a foundation plan: diagnostics contracts, instrumentation hooks, and editor UX affordances.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:55] observe — codebase restructured into packages/ since plan was filed. LSP in packages/spw-lsp/src/, seed in packages/spw-seed/src/, runtime in packages/spw-runtime/src/. Lore-era baseline no longer reachable.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:56] revise — rebase target updated to main@3b1747c4. File paths updated to packages/ layout. Expanded from 5 to 12 commits to create surface area for each DX station: diagnostic registry, seed hooks, runtime hooks, LSP propagation, CLI diagnostics, editor integration, and documentation.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:57] decide — resolve dx-scope: priority order is (1) parser/seed diagnostics (most visible to new users), (2) LSP server (editor experience), (3) CLI (installation troubleshooting), (4) runtime interpreter (deeper debugging). This matches the spiritual testing path: author → seed → runtime → editor → publish.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:58] decide — site codebases need a diagnostic mode that answers: is .spw installed correctly? can the parser load? can the LSP start? does the extension connect? Each station should emit a structured health check.
 >>[2026-03-27 00:59] taste — each commit in this plan should produce a concrete artifact that external developers can encounter: an error code they can search for, a status bar indicator they can read, a CLI flag they can use. More commits = more contact surfaces.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:18] revise — reposition this branch as the DX contract lane inside a broader ecology effort. Commit 1 serializes station names; after that, seed, LSP, CLI, and editor work can proceed in parallel without inventing their own diagnostic vocabulary.
 >>[2026-03-27 13:19] taste — ecological invigoration here means a site codebase encounters one coherent station model across install, editor, CLI, and docs rather than four unrelated troubleshooting dialects.
}

^["open"]{
 # resolved: dx-scope — priority order: seed → LSP → CLI → runtime; see stream 2026-03-27 00:57
}

